    "title": "Hot Potato Game",
    "category": "Queue",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "problemStatement": "There are N players standing in a circle, numbered from 1 to N. Starting from player 1, a token is passed clockwise exactly K times. The player holding the token after the K-th pass is eliminated. The process continues with the next player until only one player remains. Return the number of the winning player.",
    "input": "Integer N Integer K",
    "output": "The winning player's number.",
    "constraints": "1 <= N <= 10^5 1 <= K <= 10^5"
